course: dictionary
lesson: 3650
title: Firewood and the words around it
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Donkeys were tamed in north-east Africa about 7,000 years ago, and tens of millions still carry water, crops and firewood today.» Look at the words around firewood. Donkeys carry water and crops, and firewood is something else they carry, so it must be a thing you can load and carry.
explain: Firewood is made of two words joined together: fire and wood. It means wood that has been cut into pieces so it can burn in a fire, a stove or a fireplace. The word tells you what it is for.
explain: Firewood is a noun with no plural. You do not say «firewoods». Instead, say «a pile of firewood», «a bundle of firewood» or «some firewood».
fact: Firewood means wood cut into pieces to burn in a fire, a stove or a fireplace.
fact: Firewood is a compound word: fire + wood.
fact: «Firewood» has no plural, so say «a pile of firewood», not «firewoods».
fact: Useful phrases: «chop firewood», «gather firewood», «a stack of firewood».
fact: Safety: keep firewood dry, stack it away from the house, and never burn painted or treated wood.
exercise: In this sentence, what is firewood? «Donkeys ... carry water, crops and firewood today.» | Water kept in a bucket | *Wood cut into pieces to burn | Animal fur | A kind of donkey food
exercise: Which phrase uses firewood correctly? | *a pile of firewood | many firewoods | firewoods in a stack | two firewoods
exercise: Which is the safest way to keep firewood for a fire? | Burn old painted wood from the fence | Leave it out in the rain next to the back door | *Keep it dry and stack it away from the house | Pile it right against the wall of the house and forget it
test: Which word means wood cut into pieces to burn in a fire? | Bark | Sawdust | Ice | *Firewood
test: Which sentence uses firewood correctly? | We gathered three firewoods for the campfire. | *We gathered some firewood for the campfire. | We gathered a firewoods for the campfire. | We gathered firewoods for the campfires.
exam: Why should you never burn painted or treated wood in a campfire or stove? | Painted wood is too hard to chop | It makes the fire burn too cold | It makes the wood too heavy to carry | *Paint and treatments can give off harmful smoke
